# Sales Report Rules

**Every uploaded or replaced sales CSV must follow these rules** — bundled seed (`data/reports/Sales-Report.csv`), Data Analyst upload, and API `POST /api/reports`.

## Excluded rows — remove from the report entirely

These rows are treated as **deleted** from the sales report. They must **not** appear in Top 20, Top vendors, stores, departments, designs, metal/class, margins, revenue totals, rank-detail, voice, or chat.

### Exclusion rules (match on SKU # or Item #)

| Rule | Reason |
|------|--------|
| `ITEM` | Placeholder / custom order / special order lines |
| `250000` | CBE recycling fee |
| Starts with `MLB-` | Mulberry lifetime / care plans |
| `JVS-200940` | Watch battery service (repair, not product) |
| `217365`, `217286`, `159004` | Legacy excluded SKUs |
| `WATCH WINDER`, `WATCH WINDER-1`, vendor model starts with `WATCH WINDER` | Complimentary / no-warranty watch winder (not product revenue) |
| `229080` | White bag with blue ribbon — packaging / $0 sale lines |
| Description / style / vendor model contains `Pad [s]` (case-insensitive) | Earring pad / screwback pad accessory lines — not jewelry product revenue |
| Blank / empty **Department** | Incomplete line — drop the row |
| **Matched return / void pair** | Negative qty **or** negative amount + matching sale with **same store**, **same calendar date**, **same absolute Total/net**, same SKU/vendor model — drop **both** legs (prefer same Transaction #). Never void-pair across days (keeps daily nets aligned with Excel). |
| **Exchange (same Transaction #, different SKU)** | After void-pair removal, keep negative-qty lines when that Transaction # still has a sale leg — Net Sales includes both (e.g. net 650 + (−324.83) = 325.17). **Units sold** count positive qty only. Cross-txn void pairing must not remove these exchange returns. |
| **Stand-alone returns (negative qty)** | After void-pair removal, drop negative-qty lines whose Transaction # has **no** remaining sale leg (sales dashboard is sales-only). |

## Soft-hidden from Top Vendor Models only

These still count in Net Sales / store / vendor / department totals, but must **not** appear in Top Vendor Models / top-product lists:

| Rule | Reason |
|------|--------|
| Vendor model `WG2787` | Hidden from top vendor models (still in net sales) |
| Vendor model `WG670` | Threaded earring post — findings; hidden from top vendor models (still in net sales) |
| Vendor model `2200-2218` | Screwback earring back / pad — findings; hidden from top vendor models (still in net sales) |

### Implementation (do not bypass on upload)

- **Single source of truth:** `isExcludedSalesSku()` + `isExcludedSalesRow()` + `isHiddenFromTopVendorModelsRow()` / `filterTopProductSkus()` + `dropMatchedSalesReturnPairs()` + `dropStandaloneNegativeQtyReturns()` + `filterExcludedSalesRows()` in `src/lib/utils.ts`
- **On every summarize/upload:** filter `periodRows` (and `compareRows`) in `summarizeVendorPos()` via `filterExcludedSalesRows()`
- **On rank-detail / visualizations / sales version refresh:** filter rows the same way
- Cached sales versions rebuild when `SALES_EXCLUSION_RULES_VERSION` bumps

When adding exclusions, update `src/lib/utils.ts` only.

## Profit / margin

- When the CSV includes **Profit Amount**, use that column as row `margin` (do **not** recompute as Total − Inventory Cost). Margin % = Profit Amount ÷ Total.
- Fallback only if Profit Amount is absent: `margin = Total − Inventory Cost`.

## Bundled default report

- File: `data/reports/Sales-Report.csv`
- Seeded via `src/lib/reports/store.ts`; app refreshes `.data/reports/` when the file changes
- Current seed window: **2025-01-01 → 2026-08-07**

## Daily append format (always)

Going forward, daily sales files use the Umair / POS export shape. Treat this as the canonical daily append format on upload (`POST /api/reports`, Data Analyst, merge into live report).

| Column in CSV | App field |
|---|---|
| `Item  #` | **SKU** (`sku` / `itemNumber`) — same as `SKU #` when present |
| `VendorModel1` | **Vendor model** |
| `Image Dir.` | Product image path — **always store/resolve as `.webp`** (replace `.jpg` / `.jpeg` / `.png` / `.gif`) |
| `Profit Amount` | Row margin (see Profit / margin above) |
| `Transaction Date` | Day key for append/replace-same-day merge |

### Empty spacer columns

Daily files often have blank header cells between fields (double commas). Always run `normalizeDailySalesCsv()` before parse/merge/save — collapse columns whose header is empty; do not invent names for blank headers.

### Implementation

- `src/lib/reports/normalize-daily-sales-csv.ts` — collapse empty columns + Image Dir → webp
- `src/lib/reports/product-image.ts` — `normalizeSalesImageDir()` / `preferWebpFilename()`
- `src/lib/reports/vendor-pos.ts` — maps `Item  #` → SKU, `VendorModel1` → vendor model (also accepts historical `SKU #` / `Vendor Model`; prefers non-empty); normalizes `imageDir` at parse
- `src/lib/reports/merge-sales-csv.ts` — append by Transaction Date (same day replaces); copies `Item  #` → `SKU #` and `VendorModel1` → `Vendor Model` when merging into the live seed
- Apply normalize on every sales upload path (`api/reports`, `summarizeCsvText`)
- Self-check: `npx tsx scripts/check-daily-sales-csv.ts`

## Salespersons

- POS codes in the Salespersons cell (e.g. `SN/65% - SP/35%`) are mapped to real names via `data/salespersons/salespersons.csv` (`src/lib/sales/salesperson-directory.ts`).
- Rankings / rank-detail show **Name (CODE)** when the code exists in the directory.